@startuml qnx_dispatch_server_destroy_connection_activity
title QnxDispatchServer - connection destruction

start
:Enter ServerConnection destructor in its destruction caller;
:GetQnxDispatchServer() through the native OCB binding;
if (user_data_ is engaged?) then (yes)
    if (UserData holds a handler unique pointer?) then (handler)
        :Invoke handler->OnDisconnect(connection);
    else (server callback)
        :Invoke server.disconnect_callback_(connection);
    endif
else (pending/unaccepted)
    :Skip application disconnect delivery;
endif
:Clear send_queue_ intrusive membership;
:Clear notify_pool_ intrusive membership;
:Destroy members, including outgoing storage and UserData;
stop

legend
    ProcessDisconnect resets self_ and invokes destruction of an accepted object.
    Failed admission also destroys its locally owned pending object.
    The server lookup precedes the UserData presence check in the implementation.
    No send mutex, empty-callback guard or queued-message flush is added here.
    RequestDisconnect is a distinct public method whose current body is empty.
endlegend

@enduml
